IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `amd-act`
IMPORT `amd-offences`

-- Advance Medical Directive Act 1996, ss 11 to 21 -- worked cases.

§ `Fixtures`

-- Interest fixtures, defined here so this file stands alone rather than
-- depending on amd-cases.l4.
`no interests` MEANS Interests WITH
    `a beneficiary under the patient's will or any policy of insurance` IS FALSE
    `has an interest under an instrument under which the patient is donor, settlor or grantor` IS FALSE
    `would be entitled to an interest in the estate on the patient's intestacy` IS FALSE
    `would be entitled to the patient's provident fund moneys on death` IS FALSE
    `has registered an objection under section 10(1)` IS FALSE

`a beneficiary under the will` MEANS Interests WITH
    `a beneficiary under the patient's will or any policy of insurance` IS TRUE
    `has an interest under an instrument under which the patient is donor, settlor or grantor` IS FALSE
    `would be entitled to an interest in the estate on the patient's intestacy` IS FALSE
    `would be entitled to the patient's provident fund moneys on death` IS FALSE
    `has registered an objection under section 10(1)` IS FALSE

`only an intestacy entitlement` MEANS Interests WITH
    `a beneficiary under the patient's will or any policy of insurance` IS FALSE
    `has an interest under an instrument under which the patient is donor, settlor or grantor` IS FALSE
    `would be entitled to an interest in the estate on the patient's intestacy` IS TRUE
    `would be entitled to the patient's provident fund moneys on death` IS FALSE
    `has registered an objection under section 10(1)` IS FALSE

`Wong, aged 45` MEANS Person WITH
    `name` IS "Wong"
    `age in years` IS 45
    `mentally disordered` IS FALSE

`a practitioner entitled only on intestacy` MEANS MedicalPractitioner WITH
    `who` IS `Wong, aged 45`
    `is a specialist` IS TRUE
    `interests` IS `only an intestacy entitlement`
    `has registered an objection under section 10(1)` IS FALSE

GIVEN `procured` IS A BOOLEAN, `forged` IS A BOOLEAN, `concealed` IS A BOOLEAN, `wilful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Section14Conduct
DECIDE `conduct` `procured` `forged` `concealed` `wilful` IS
    Section14Conduct WITH
        `procured the execution of a directive by deception, fraud, misstatement, unconscionable conduct or undue influence` IS `procured`
        `falsified or forged the directive of another person` IS `forged`
        `concealed or withheld personal knowledge of a revocation` IS `concealed`
        `the concealment was wilful` IS `wilful`

`no wrongdoing` MEANS `conduct` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§§ `11 to 18 -- the questions this Act does not answer`

-- Five of the eight questions below are ones the Act expressly declines to
-- answer. Only the last is its own.
#ASSERT `this Act answers the question` `whether a directive may be acted on`
#ASSERT NOT `this Act answers the question` `whether palliative care may be given or withheld`
#ASSERT NOT `this Act answers the question` `whether a person may refuse medical or surgical treatment`
#ASSERT NOT `this Act answers the question` `whether euthanasia or abetment of suicide is permitted`
#ASSERT NOT `this Act answers the question` `whether making a directive affects a policy of insurance`

-- s 17(1): a directive permits the dying process to take its course and
-- authorises nothing that causes or accelerates death.
#ASSERT `the act is outside anything this Act authorises` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the act is outside anything this Act authorises` FALSE

§§ `14 -- the three limbs, and the wilfulness in limb (c)`

#ASSERT `an offence under section 14(1) is made out` (`conduct` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `an offence under section 14(1) is made out` (`conduct` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 14(1) is made out` `no wrongdoing`

-- Limb (c) alone carries a mental element. Concealing a revocation without
-- wilfulness is not the offence; (a) and (b) have no such qualification.
#ASSERT `an offence under section 14(1) is made out` (`conduct` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 14(1) is made out` (`conduct` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)

§§ `14(2) -- forfeiture without a conviction, on a FOURTH version of the list`

-- s 14(2) forfeits the interest of a person who "IS GUILTY of an offence under
-- subsection (1) (WHETHER OR NOT HE OR SHE HAS BEEN CONVICTED)". The rule reads
-- the conduct, not a conviction.
#ASSERT `the interest is forfeited under section 14(2)` (`conduct` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `a beneficiary under the will`
#ASSERT NOT `the interest is forfeited under section 14(2)` `no wrongdoing` `a beneficiary under the will`

-- THE LIST AGAIN. s 14(2) names four interests: will or insurance, instrument,
-- intestacy, provident fund. That is the s 3(3) witness list MINUS the
-- registered objection -- and so a FOURTH different version of the same list.
-- An intestacy entitlement forfeits here, is a bar to witnessing under
-- s 3(3)(c), and is NOT a disqualification under s 9(9) or s 10(4).
#ASSERT `the interest is forfeited under section 14(2)` (`conduct` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `only an intestacy entitlement`
#ASSERT NOT `the witness is competent under section 3(3)` (Witness WITH `who` IS `Wong, aged 45`, `is a medical practitioner` IS FALSE, `is the patient's own or chosen practitioner` IS FALSE, `interests` IS `only an intestacy entitlement`)
#ASSERT NOT `section 9(9) disqualifies the practitioner from certifying` `a practitioner entitled only on intestacy`
#ASSERT NOT `section 10(4) disqualifies the practitioner from acting` `a practitioner entitled only on intestacy`

-- A person with no relevant interest forfeits nothing, however they behaved.
#ASSERT NOT `the interest is forfeited under section 14(2)` (`conduct` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `no interests`

§§ `14(3) and 14(4) -- a charge freezes, a conviction revokes`

-- A CHARGE stops anyone acting on the directive until its validity is
-- ascertained; it does not take a conviction.
#ASSERT `section 14(3) bars acting on the directive` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 14(3) bars acting on the directive` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 14(3) bars acting on the directive` FALSE FALSE

-- A CONVICTION deems the directive revoked outright.
#ASSERT `the directive is deemed revoked under section 14(4)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the directive is deemed revoked under section 14(4)` FALSE

§§ `15 -- the prohibition on asking, and its three-part exception`

GIVEN `has care` IS A BOOLEAN, `asked` IS A BOOLEAN, `responsible` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `good practice` IS A BOOLEAN, `in relationship` IS A BOOLEAN, `public education` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN EnquiryFacts
DECIDE `an enquiry` `has care` `asked` `responsible` `good practice` `in relationship` `public education` IS
    EnquiryFacts WITH
        `the person has or will likely have the medical care of the patient` IS `has care`
        `the person asked or enquired whether a directive has been or will be made` IS `asked`
        `the person is the medical practitioner responsible for the patient's care` IS `responsible`
        `the discussion was consistent with good medical practice` IS `good practice`
        `the discussion was held in the context of the practitioner-patient relationship` IS `in relationship`
        `the discussion was in furtherance of the purposes of public education` IS `public education`

#ASSERT `the person contravenes section 15(1)` (`an enquiry` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- The exception needs the responsible practitioner AND all three conditions.
#ASSERT NOT `the person contravenes section 15(1)` (`an enquiry` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the person contravenes section 15(1)` (`an enquiry` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the person contravenes section 15(1)` (`an enquiry` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- Someone with no part in the patient's care is outside s 15(1) altogether.
#ASSERT NOT `the person contravenes section 15(1)` (`an enquiry` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- s 15(3): confidentiality lifts on the s 9 determination -- the same moment the
-- register may be disclosed under s 6(3)(c).
#ASSERT `the information must be kept confidential` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the information must be kept confidential` TRUE

§§ `16 -- both directions are caught`

-- An insurer may not demand a directive, and may not forbid one either.
#ASSERT `an offence under section 16(1) is committed` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `an offence under section 16(1) is committed` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 16(1) is committed` FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Only where it is a condition of insurance or of medical or health care.
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 16(1) is committed` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- s 16(2) severs the condition; it does not void the policy.
#ASSERT `the condition is void to that extent under section 16(2)` TRUE FALSE TRUE

§§ `19 -- good faith AND absence of negligence`

#ASSERT `the practitioner is protected by section 19(1)` `whether the patient is suffering from a terminal illness` TRUE TRUE
-- Good faith alone is not enough.
#ASSERT NOT `the practitioner is protected by section 19(1)` `whether the patient is suffering from a terminal illness` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the practitioner is protected by section 19(1)` `whether the patient is suffering from a terminal illness` FALSE TRUE
-- And only for the four decisions s 19(1) names.
#ASSERT NOT `the practitioner is protected by section 19(1)` `some other decision` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `the practitioner is protected by section 19(1)` `whether a directive was valid` TRUE TRUE

-- s 19(2) is a different test: ignorance of the revocation, not good faith.
#ASSERT `the person is protected by section 19(2)` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the person is protected by section 19(2)` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the person is protected by section 19(2)` FALSE FALSE

§§ `20 -- causation, and what it does not reach`

#ASSERT `the withholding does not constitute a cause of death` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- The rule is conditional on the directive having been VALIDLY made.
#ASSERT NOT `the withholding does not constitute a cause of death` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the withholding does not constitute a cause of death` TRUE FALSE TRUE

-- s 20(2): a negligent terminal-illness decision is outside the protection --
-- and by s 19(1) the practitioner loses that protection too, on the same fact.
#ASSERT `section 20 leaves the practitioner exposed` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 20 leaves the practitioner exposed` FALSE

§§ `21 -- composition`

#ASSERT `the offence may be compounded for that sum` TRUE 1000
#ASSERT NOT `the offence may be compounded for that sum` TRUE 1001
-- An offence not prescribed as compoundable cannot be compounded at all.
#ASSERT NOT `the offence may be compounded for that sum` FALSE 100
